speaker: drop stale DAC requests from the worklet (port of upstream PR #1661)

Upstream: https://github.com/copy/v86/pull/1661 (issue #1660, "SB16 replays already-played
DMA blocks after the main thread stalls"), open and not merged in v86 0.5.473. The upstream
change is on src/browser/speaker.js (SpeakerWorkletDAC and its DACProcessor worklet); this is
the same change applied to the compiled build/libv86.js of the npm package, where the Closure
compiler renamed SpeakerWorkletDAC to `kb` and DACProcessor to `h`:

- the worklet counts the buffers it received (`received_count`) and sends that count with
  every "pump" request;
- the main side counts the buffers it sent (`sent_count`, incremented only when a buffer is
  actually posted) and ignores a "pump" whose count is not the current one: after a stall of
  the thread that runs v86 the worklet has queued many requests, and serving each of them
  would advance the SB16 DMA past what the guest refilled (trial E5: `aplay` dies with an I/O
  error after a 300 ms stall without this guard; completes without replay with it).

Measured in docs/essais/e5-son.md. To be dropped when a published v86 contains the merge.

